+---
+kind: upgrade-guide
+description: Callers of primary-runtime queries must handle absent Python paths for explicitly selected Node-only payloads.
+---
+
+# Node-only primary runtime
+
+English | [中文](guide.zh.md)
+
+## Change
+
+A `schemaVersion: 2` primary-runtime manifest supplies Node without Python. `PrimaryRuntimeManifest` discriminates Python and Node-only metadata. `WorkspaceDependencies.python` and `pythonPackages` may be absent; existing Python payloads still return them. Node-only resources are opt-in and do not replace Python-based Office authoring workflows.
+
+## Migration
+
+1. In callers of `resolvePrimaryRuntime`, `installPrimaryRuntime`, or `load_workspace_dependencies`, require the interpreter needed by the operation. Check Python paths before Python operations; use the returned Node path for Node operations.
+2. To prepare a Node-only carrier, run `pnpm run prepare:primary-runtime --target <target> --output <directory> --node-only`. Do not combine it with `--python-only`. Keep the existing Python payload for Python Office authoring until a Node workflow is provided.
+3. Verify `runtime.json` has `schemaVersion: 2` and no `python`, the resource tree has no Python directory, and the native-target smoke executes Node and pnpm. See the [payload reference](../../../../packages/skill/tool-workspace-dependencies/README.md).
